<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Pitt the Elder</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1708–1778</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as William Pitt, 1st Earl of Chatham, Pitt the Elder</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Pitt the Elder, later 1st Earl of Chatham, was a British statesman who led the government during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>. From 1757 he concentrated British strength on naval power and colonial conquest while subsidising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and the 'year of victories' of 1759 brought the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> and gains in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. He was Prime Minister again from 1766 to 1768 and father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-pitt-the-younger">William Pitt the Younger</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-pitt-the-elder.jpg" alt="William Pitt the Elder" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Studio of William Hoare · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Pitt,_1st_Earl_of_Chatham_by_William_Hoare.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
